## Stance on Social Media

The P3D project is fine with sharing information online. In fact, we ENCOURAGE sharing your contributions online, but there are a few rules that we’d want you to abide by.

- **Only share YOUR contributions to the project.** What does this mean? It means literally what it says; only share what you have worked/helped with, not just generally showcasing the project. We want to leave that for our Milestone videos (see [P3D Roadmap](/roadmap/))
- **Don’t discuss/reveal LOCKED TOPICS online**. What are locked topics? They are topics that the team wants to keep a surprise for our own Milestone videos. You can check if a topic is locked/not locked by viewing the “Locked Topics” under each milestone on the [P3D Roadmap](/roadmap/)
- **Add a link/mention to the project** (ideally the Discord link). This is just so that we get more exposure (and hopefully team members!).
  - [https://discord.gg/CQnkc5gS6a](https://discord.gg/CQnkc5gS6a)
  - Use the ***#thep3dproject #persona3dual #persona3 #persona*** hashtags
  - Add a link to your social media post in the #socials channel, so the official accounts can repost!
- **Don’t act as a “representative” of the team** **to external stakeholders without approval**. What does this mean? It means you, 1. CAN talk about the project, milestones, etc., but 2. CANNOT contact people outside of the team for items that impact development (ex. Asking others about using their music/videos/assets) without approval from the team itself. This is not doing us a favour!
- Be respectful, don’t associate the project politically, yada yada, the common sense stuff

